R-3m, NMC811 prototype) 83	      - olivine LiMPO4 (Pnma, LiFePO4 prototype) 84	      - spinel LiM2O4 (Fd-3m, LiMn2O4 prototype) 85	      - tavorite phosphate LiM(PO4)F (P-1, LiVPO4F prototype) 86	      - tavorite sulfate LiM(SO4)F (P-1, LiFeSO4F cell + tavorite framework coordinates) 87	      - NASICON Li3M2(PO4)3 (P2₁/c, Li3V2(PO4)3 prototype, COD 2237423) 88	    Other frameworks (oxyfluorides Li2MO2F, Li2CoPO4F/Li2NiPO4F, ...) have no template → 89	    explicit error. 90	    """ 91	    framework = _framework(formula) 92	    if framework == "tavorite_phosphate": 93	        return _build_tavorite(formula, sulfate=False) 94	    if framework == "tavorite_sulfate": 95	        return _build_tavorite(formula, sulfate=True) 96	    if framework == "nasicon": 97	        return _build_nasicon(formula) 98	    if framework == "olivine": 99	        return _build_olivine(formula) 100	    if framework == "spinel": 101	        return _build_spinel(formula) 102	    tm = _tm_fractions(formula) 103	    struct = _base_structure() 104	    tm_sites = [ 105	        i for i, site in enumerate(struct) if site.specie.symbol not in ("Li", "O") 106	    ] 107	    counts = _largest_remainder(tm, len(tm_sites)) 108	    rng = np.random.default_rng(_seed(formula)) 109	    order = rng.permutation(len(tm_sites)) 110	    assignment: list[str] = [] 111	    for sym, k in counts.items(): 112	        assignment += [sym] * k 113	    rng.shuffle(assignment) 114	    for pos, sym in zip(order, assignment): 115	        struct.replace(tm_sites[pos], sym) 116	    return struct, counts, tm_sites 117	 118	 119	def _framework(formula: str) -> str: 120	    """Stoichiometry → framework name (strict; raises ValueError on no match — never guesses).""" 121	    comp = Composition(formula) 122	    els = {str(k): float(v) for k, v in comp.items()} 123	    tm_total = sum(v for k, v in els.items() if k not in ("Li", "O", "P", "S", "F")) 124	 125	    def eq(name: str, value: float) -> bool: 126	        return abs(els.get(name, 0.0) - value) < 1e-6 127	 128	    if eq("Li", 1.0) and eq("O", 4.0) and eq("F", 1.0) and tm_total > 1e-9: 129	        if eq("P", 1.0) and not els.get("S", 0.0): 130	            return "tavorite_phosphate" 131	        if eq("S", 1.0) and not els.get("P", 0.0): 132	            return "tavorite_sulfate" 133	    if eq("Li", 3.0) and eq("P", 3.0) and eq("O", 12.0) and abs(tm_total - 2.0) < 1e-6: 134	        return "nasicon" 135	    if eq("Li", 1.0) and eq("O", 4.0) and eq("P", 1.0) \ 136	            and not els.get("F", 0.0) and not els.get("S", 0.0): 137	        return "olivine" 138	    if eq("Li", 1.0) and eq("O", 4.0) and abs(tm_total - 2.0) < 1e-6 \ 139	            and not els.get("P", 0.0) and not els.get("S", 0.0) and not els.get("F", 0.0): 140	        return "spinel" 141	    if eq("Li", 1.0) and eq("O", 2.0) and abs(tm_total - 1.0) < 1e-6 \ 142	            and not els.get("P", 0.0) and not els.get("S", 0.0) and not els.get("F", 0.0): 143	        return "layered" 144	    raise ValueError( 145	        f"unsupported framework for {formula}: supported are layered LiMO2, olivine LiMPO4, " 146	        f"spinel LiM2O4, tavorite LiM(PO4)F, tavorite LiM(SO4)F, NASICON Li3M2(PO4)3" 147	    ) 148	 149	 150	def _build_olivine(formula: str) -> tuple[Structure, dict[str, int], list[int]]: 151	    """Olivine Pnma (LiFePO4 standard parameters: a=10.332 b=6.010 c=4.694 Å). 152	    Representative coordinates (Wyckoff): Li 4a (0,0,0); M 4c (0.218,0.25,0.202); 153	    P 4c (0.0946,0.25,0.0619); O 4c×2 + 8d → 28-atom primitive cell (from_spacegroup).""" 154	    struct = Structure.from_spacegroup( 155	        "Pnma", 156	        Lattice.orthorhombic(10.332, 6.010, 4.694), 157	        ["Li", "M", "P", "O", "O", "O"], 158	        [[0, 0, 0], 159	         [0.218, 0.25, 0.202], 160	         [0.0946, 0.25, 0.0619], 161	         [0.0984, 0.25, 0.7427], 162	         [0.0450, 0.25, 0.2849], 163	         [0.0859, 0.0358, 0.5330]], 164	    ) 165	    tm_sites = [i for i, site in enumerate(struct) if site.specie.symbol == "M"] 166	    tm = {str(k): float(v) for k, v in Composition(formula).items() 167	          if str(k) not in ("Li", "O", "P", "Si", "F")} 168	    total = sum(tm.values()) 169	    tm = {k: v / total for k, v in tm.items()}  # normalized (olivine M site = 1.0) 170	    counts = _largest_remainder(tm, len(tm_sites)) 171	    rng = np.random.default_rng(_seed(formula)) 172	    order = rng.permutation(len(tm_sites)) 173	    assignment: list[str] = [] 174	    for sym, k in counts.items(): 175	        assignment += [sym] * k 176	    rng.shuffle(assignment) 177	    for pos, sym in zip(order, assignment): 178	        struct.replace(tm_sites[pos], sym) 179	    return struct, counts, tm_sites 180	 181	 182	def _build_spinel(formula: str) -> tuple[Structure, dict[str, int], list[int]]: 183	    """Spinel Fd-3m (LiMn2O4, COD 1513964: a=8.251 Å; 56-atom cell = 8 Li / 16 M / 32 O). 184	 185	    **Coordinate provenance and a corrected bug (2026-09-10).** The authoritative COD entry 186	    describes this structure in the Fd-3m origin-choice-2 setting: Li on 8a (1/8,1/8,1/8), 187	    M on 16d (1/2,1/2,1/2), O on 32e with x=0.263. pymatgen's `from_spacegroup` applies the 188	    *origin-choice-1* setting, in which those same fractional coordinates generate 16 and 8 189	    sites respectively — i.e. the previous code built Li16 M8 O32 (Li2MO4) with Li in 190	    octahedral holes and M ~3.4 Å from any oxygen. Its "voltages" (7.8-9.0 V) were artefacts 191	    of that wrong structure. The setting-correct assignment used here is 192	    Li 8-fold (1/2,1/2,1/2), M 16-fold (1/8,1/8,1/8), O 32e x=0.3622 (= 0.625 - 0.2628). 193	    Verified against the COD entry: identical cell volume and coordination spectra — 194	    Li 4 O at 1.97 Å (tetrahedral), M 6 O at 1.96 Å (octahedral). 195	    """ 196	    struct = Structure.from_spacegroup( 197	        "Fd-3m", 198	        Lattice.cubic(8.251), 199	        ["Li", "M", "O"], 200	        [[0.5, 0.5, 0.5], 201	         [0.125,