nPO₄F (tavorite): LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄ (LMNP) and LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄F (LMNPF). - Li intercalation voltage increased to **4.27 V for LMNP** and **5.23 V for the tavorite LMNPF**. - Calculated Li migration barrier for LMNPF was **0.4 eV**, lower than that of pristine LiMnPO₄F. - After Li insertion, the MNPF unit-cell volume increased by ~8%, less than pristine MnPO₄F.  **Note on scope:** The search results do not contain a study explicitly on "LiNiPO₄F" tavorite; the closest Ni-containing systems reported are Li₂NiPO₄F (a related fluorophosphate 5 V cathode) and the Ni-substituted tavorite LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄F. One additional result covers tavorite LiFe₁₋ₓVₓPO₄F solid solutions, but that is an experimental study focused on Fe/V redox tuning via inductive effects, not Ni or DFT voltage calculations.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
