010.1021/acsami.9b23367.pdf#4%231"},{"title":"Download Citation","url":"https://pubs.acs.org/action/showCitFormats?doi=10.1021/acsami.9b23367&href=/doi/10.1021/acsami.9b23367?goto=supporting-info"}]  The search results confirm the paper you're looking for and its key finding about LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄F.  ## Paper Details  **Title:** "Density Functional Theory Investigation of Mixed Transition Metals in Olivine and Tavorite Cathode Materials for Li-Ion Batteries"  **Authors:** Muhammad Hilmy Alfaruqi, Seokhun Kim, Sohyun Park, Seulgi Lee, Jun Lee, Jang-Yeon Hwang, Yang-Kook Sun, Jaekook Kim  **Journal:** ACS Applied Materials & Interfaces, 2020, 12(14), 16376–16386 **DOI:** 10.1021/acsami.9b23367 | **PMID:** 32186369  ## Key Findings Relevant to Your Query  The study used first-principles density functional theory (DFT) to investigate Ni-substituted olivine LiMnPO₄ (LMP) and tavorite LiMnPO₄F (LMPF), i.e., **LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄ (LMNP)** and **LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄F (LMNPF)**, along with their delithiated phases Mn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄ (MNP) and Mn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄F (MNPF).  - **Li intercalation voltage:** The calculated voltage increased with Ni substitution to **4.27 V for LMNP** and **5.23 V for LMNPF** — matching the 5.23 V figure in your query for the tavorite LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄F. - **Structural change:** After Li insertion, the MNPF unit-cell volume increased by about 8%, which is lower than that of pristine MnPO₄F. - **Li migration barrier:** Calculated to be **0.4 eV for LMNPF**, lower than that of LMPF. - **Thermodynamic stability:** Calculated mixing energies (ΔE_mix) were negative for both LMNP and LMNPF, suggesting they are thermodynamically favored and could potentially be synthesized. The authors noted that, to their knowledge, there had been no report on the synthesis of tavorite LMNPF at that time. - **Computational approach:** Calculations were performed with the Quantum-Espresso package using PAW pseudopotentials, the PBEsol GGA functional with Hubbard U correction (U = 3.9 eV for Mn; 6.1 eV for Ni), a 50 Ry plane-wave cutoff, and the BFGS algorithm.  **Keywords:** olivine; tavorite; mixed-transition metal; lithium-ion battery; density functional theory; first-principle calculations  The authors conclude the study may provide insights for developing LMNP and LMNPF cathode materials in LIB applications. Affiliations include Chonnam National University, Universitas Teknologi Sumbawa, and Hanyang University, with funding from the National Research Foundation of Korea (NRF).   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
