[tool_result]Web search results for query: ""LiNiPO4F" synthesis hydrothermal prepared experimental cathode report"  Links: [{"title":"Как следует из табл","url":"https://sibran.ru/upload/iblock/432/4320d901ae64d6fee190aa82fbce5d53.pdf#4#2"},{"title":"Synthesis of cathode material for lithium battery - - FIG","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US20240150177A1/en#3"},{"title":"Lian Wan;Tingrui Liu;Xing Zhou;Feng Chen; - [期刊论文][Full-length article]","url":"https://www.socolar.com/Article/Index?aid=100085494673&amp;jid=100000001660#1"},{"title":"Alkali/transition metal halo-and hydroxy-phosphates and related electrode active materials - A mixture of 36.95 g (0.5 mol) of Li2CO3, 164.01 (0.334 mol) of Ni3(PO4)2.7H2O, and 44.11 g (0.334 mol) of (NH4)2HPO4 is made, u...","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US8367036#7"},{"title":"万方数据知识服务平台 - 摘要：基于碱金属离子嵌/脱的氟磷酸盐材料(Li2MPO4F，M=Fe，Co，Mn)因本身结构稳定,安全性能好,工作电压高,能够满足当前对锂电池正极材料高容量与高能量密度的要求,其中,Li2CoPO4F在当前可行性正极材料中,具备最高的工作电压平台(4.8V...","url":"https://s.wanfangdata.com.cn/thesis?q=%E5%AF%BC%E5%B8%88%3A%22%E5%86%AF%E5%AD%A3%E5%86%9B%22%20%E5%AD%A6%E4%BD%8D%E6%8E%88%E4%BA%88%E5%8D%95%E4%BD%8D%3A%22%E6%B5%8E%E5%8D%97%E5%A4%A7%E5%AD%A6%22#6"},{"title":"Alkali/Transition Metal Halo-And Hydroxy-Phosphates And Related Electrode Active Materials - Eureka | Patsnap","url":"https://eureka-patsnap-com.sutd.idm.oclc.org/patent-US20070190425A1"},{"title":"Alkali/transition metal halo-and hydroxy-modified phosphates and related electrode active materials - - LiNiPO 4 + 2.833 H 2 O + 0.667 NH 3 + 0.5 CO 2 A mixture of 36.95 g (0.5 mol) of Li 2 CO 3 , 164.01 (0.334 mol) of Ni 3 (PO 4 ...","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/EP1444744A2/en#12"}]  ## Summary  None of the provided search results reports a hydrothermal synthesis of **LiNiPO₄F** itself. The results instead concern the closely related fluorophosphate **Li₂NiPO₄F** (Li₁₊ₓNiPO₄Fₓ, x = 1), which is prepared by solid-state/mechanochemical routes, while hydrothermal methods appear only for related materials.  **Solid-state/mechanochemical synthesis of Li₂NiPO₄F and derivatives** - A LiNiPO₄ precursor is first made from Li₂CO₃, Ni₃(PO₄)₂·7H₂O, and (NH₄)₂HPO₄, pelletized, and heated at ~2 °C/min to 800 °C for 16 h in air; the Li₂NiPO₄F active material is then formed from this precursor (US20070190425A1, https://eureka-patsnap-com.sutd.idm.oclc.org/patent-US20070190425A1). A related version heats at 750 °C for 8 h in an inert atmosphere (EP1444744A2, https://patents.google.com/patent/EP1444744A2/en#12). - The resulting Li₂NiPO₄F was tested as a cathode (80% active material, 8% Super P carbon, 12% KYNAR binder) against a lithium-metal anode with 1 M LiPF₆ in EC/DMC (2:1) (US8367036, https://patents.google.com/patent/US8367036#7). - US20240150177A1 describes ball-milling LiCoₓNi₁₋ₓPO₄ with stoichiometric LiF for 12 h, pressing pellets, sintering at 750 °C for 8 h under argon flow in a covered graphite crucible, followed by rapid air quenching because the material is unstable at room temperature. XRD confirmed phase-pure Li₂NiPO₄F in the orthorhombic Pnma space group; SEM was used for morphology. The material shows a ~5.3 V redox potential, currently limited by commercial electrolyte stability (https://patents.google.com/patent/US20240150177A1/en#3). - An in situ XRD study found that Li₂CoPO₄F and Li₂NiPO₄F form from LiMPO₄ + LiF via mechanochemical activation, with Li₂NiPO₄F crystallizing at 500–550 °C (annealing at 500 °C) and Li₂CoPO₄F at 600–650 °C (650 °C); higher temperatures or slow cooling decompose these thermodynamically unstable compounds (https://sibran.ru/upload/iblock/432/4320d901ae64d6fee190aa82fbce5d53.pdf#4#2).  **Hydrothermal-related findings (but not for LiNiPO₄F)** - A thesis abstract reports that hydrothermal and solvothermal methods (water:ethanol = 1:1) can prepare **Li₂CoPO₄F**; optimal conditions were 12 h hydrothermal treatment with 600 °C calcination. Ni-doped Li₂Co₁₋ₓNiₓPO₄F (x = 0.07) showed better structural stability/reversibility and delivered 133.8 mAh g⁻¹ (https://s.wanfangdata.com.cn/thesis?q=...). This is the closest hydrothermal/experimental cathode report found, but it targets Li₂CoPO₄F and Ni-doped variants, not LiNiPO₄F. - A sol-gel + hydrothermal route was also used for a Li₃PO₄-coated, F-doped layered oxide Li₁.₂₀[Mn₀.₅₄Ni₀.₁₃Co₀.₁₃]O₁.₉₅F₀.₀₅ cathode, again not LiNiPO₄F (https://www.socolar.com/Article/Index?aid=100085494673&jid=100000001660#1).  **Bottom line:** Based only on these results, no experimental report of hydrothermally prepared LiNiPO₄F cathode material is present; the reported Li₂NiPO₄F syntheses are solid-state or mechanochemical, and hydrothermal preparation is documented only for related Li₂CoPO₄F (and Ni-doped Li₂CoPO₄F) and F-doped layered oxides.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
