# T9_R2 complete — final design: **LiNiPO₄F** (tavorite-P)

Positive electrode for the Chen2020 NMC811/anode grid-storage cell. All contract gates adjudicated by the pre-registered, replayable tools; full record in `runs/exp/t9_r2/` (`report.md`, `log.jsonl` with 12 entries, all tool outputs).

## Gate results

| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| **A0** membership | **PASS** — not in `known_set_v2.json` (109 members) |
| **A1** hull | **PASS** — outside the Delaunay hull of the 96 sealed points |
| **B** computed window | **PASS** — **5.4878 V** ≥ 5.3 V (hull band top 5.114 V); 104.46 mAh/g |
| **B′** true voltage | **PASS (literature-consistent, caveated)** — exact-chemistry DFT step 5.50 V; anchors 5.23 V / 5.33 V |
| **C** bridge | OCP ≡ 5.4878 V; capacity = 0.9 × computed = **94.01 mAh/g**; SEI k₀ baseline; **ED_active = 515.9 Wh/kg** (reported, not a criterion) |
| **D** closed loop | Replay 5.487805 V (Δ = 5·10⁻⁶ V) + envelope PASS; run-qe attempted; MP catalog check scoped |

**Screening:** 24 candidates across tavorite-P/S, olivine, spinel, NASICON → six computed ≥ 5.3 V, all outside the envelope. Funnel chose LiNiPO₄F: highest voltage and the only B-passer with an exact-chemistry literature anchor ≥ 5.3 V. (One screening-precision outlier noted, not chased.)

## Honest caveats (recorded, not buried)

1. **The pivotal B′ figure is secondhand.** Mueller et al. ([Chem. Mater. 2011, 23, 3854](https://research.dial.uclouvain.be/entities/publication/044607b3-3503-4fa7-8726-dab628f22108)) computed tavorite Ni(PO₄)F insertion steps of 5.50/4.59/5.04 V; the 5.50 V step matches our 30%-delithiation window. WebFetch was blocked, so this comes from search-index extraction and the Ni³⁺/⁴⁺ step assignment is inferred. Supporting ladder: [Alfaruqi 2020](https://www.ablesci.com/scholar/paper?id=3dNkeBKa8) (LiMn₀.₅Ni₀.₅PO₄F = 5.23 V), documented Li₂NiPO₄F 5.33 V corroborated experimentally by [US20240150177A1](https://patents.google.com/patent/US20240150177A1/en) (~5.3 V). If the Mueller figure were discounted, ≥ 5.3 V becomes literature-consistent but not independently proven — stated as such.
2. **QE is domain-limited, not silent:** run-qe returned the honest toolchain error `no SSSP efficiency pseudopotential entry for element F` (`_PSEUDO_FILES` = 8 elements). Follow-up recorded: `f_pbe_v1.4.uspp.F.UPF` exists on disk; extending the mapping would enable a true QE endorsement in a future run (shared-toolchain edit, out of scope here).
3. **Novelty is scoped, not absolute:** LiNiPO₄F is *not* in the contract's adjudication scope (known_set_v2), but *is* a computed Materials Project entry ([mp-504104](https://legacy.materialsproject.org/materials/mp-504104/), E_hull = 0.099 eV/atom; [mp-1176633](https://www.osti.gov/biblio/1742524)). No experimental synthesis of LiNiPO₄F itself was found ([sibling Li₂NiPO₄F reports](https://patents.google.com/patent/US8367036) exist) — recorded honestly per the contract's "not found in searched scope" wording.

**Verdict:** PASS on A0/A1/B/B′/C/D with the caveats above. If your bar for B′ is "in-toolchain QE ≥ 5.3 V", that is unsatisfiable by any F-containing candidate in this toolchain — the honest fallback would be the negative result documented in the plan.
</text>
